    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7744
    pr_ref:  # 7744
    description: ""  # 7744
    fields:  # 7744
      severity: "medium"  # 7744
      statement: "node.id is documented as 'lang:path:span:name:kind' (4 colons). 33818 of 33830 nodes (99.96%) follow this. 12 nodes break the format: (a) 2 npm packages with 3 colons ('typescript:npm:lit:npm_package' — missing path/span segment), (b) 2 Rust nodes with 6/8 colons because Rust namespacing uses '::' (e.g. 'rust:std::collections::HashMap:0-0:module:module'), (c) 7 Python route IDs with 5 colons because the route path '/api/items' contains a colon-style HTTP method prefix ('python:serve.py:428-428:POST:/api/items:route'), (d) 1 misc Solidity 'Not owner' carry-over. The schema id parser must handle 4 different colon-count cases without breaking."  # 7744
      root_cause: "Different code paths (NPM-package emitter, Rust namespace emitter, route emitter) format node.id without escaping or normalizing colons in the embedded path/name fields. The lang:path:span:name:kind format breaks when any field contains a literal ':'."  # 7744
